02:14:44,998 --> 02:14:51,306
[SPEAKER_06]: They gave my people the lowlands, and not much of it, just a few streets hard by the river.

267
02:14:52,547 --> 02:14:56,332
[SPEAKER_06]: Banks turned a blind eye behind the red lines, and it wasn't about the money.

268
02:14:57,233 --> 02:14:59,095
[SPEAKER_06]: Class was an irresistible force.

269
02:15:00,396 --> 02:15:02,359
[SPEAKER_06]: Race was an immovable object.

270
02:15:03,882 --> 02:15:18,899
[SPEAKER_06]: Perhaps it wasn't a written rule, but white folks knew the legal tool to keep us in our place in this mystic valley space where slaves and rum and ships had built some mansions, made some millionaires and hid some old money.

271
02:15:22,107 --> 02:15:23,968
[SPEAKER_06]: So it was hard by the mystic we went.

272
02:15:24,769 --> 02:15:26,670
[SPEAKER_06]: Muddy and a bit turned down.

273
02:15:27,350 --> 02:15:32,193
[SPEAKER_06]: The only place where one could be brown in this ancient Middlesex County town.

274
02:15:32,794 --> 02:15:33,754
[SPEAKER_06]: But we named it.

275
02:15:34,595 --> 02:15:35,335
[SPEAKER_06]: We claimed it.

276
02:15:35,876 --> 02:15:37,177
[SPEAKER_06]: We made it our own.

277
02:15:40,919 --> 02:15:48,424
[SPEAKER_06]: Even in the heat of summer when the shores were parched and the soil was rank with the decay of aquatic alchemy, we were one with the river.

278
02:15:49,407 --> 02:15:52,489
[SPEAKER_06]: We follow this flow to the lakes and the sandy beachfront.

279
02:15:53,170 --> 02:15:58,714
[SPEAKER_06]: Like our own Jordan Shore, we baptized and blessed our brothers and sisters in Christ.

280
02:15:58,975 --> 02:16:07,822
[SPEAKER_06]: We caught the little fishes to go with our loaves of bread and became the teeming multitude who our Lord Jesus fed, hired by the mystic.

281
02:16:11,150 --> 02:16:12,411
[SPEAKER_06]: We became community.

282
02:16:14,091 --> 02:16:15,412
[SPEAKER_06]: We commanded unity.

283
02:16:15,452 --> 02:16:20,034
[SPEAKER_06]: We embraced the village and raised up our children in the way they should go.

284
02:16:26,657 --> 02:16:31,179
[SPEAKER_06]: As the river ebbs and flows, the tide will turn and our fortune grows.

285
02:16:31,439 --> 02:16:33,420
[SPEAKER_06]: A few more streets become our home.

286
02:16:33,860 --> 02:16:36,762
[SPEAKER_06]: Houses on Sharon join Kin on Jerome.

287
02:16:37,122 --> 02:16:39,743
[SPEAKER_06]: From Duggar Park to the railroad tracks.

288
02:16:40,896 --> 02:16:43,239
[SPEAKER_06]: The landed folk make more room for blacks.

289
02:16:44,081 --> 02:16:46,043
[SPEAKER_06]: The color line recedes a bit.

290
02:16:46,304 --> 02:16:48,707
[SPEAKER_06]: Church and school and center sit.

291
02:16:48,968 --> 02:16:53,033
[SPEAKER_06]: The ville becomes the heart of it, hard by the mystic shore.

292
02:17:14,542 --> 02:17:43,705
[SPEAKER_06]: ♪ Now the worm has surely turned ♪ ♪ And folks who left have surely learned ♪ ♪ Things couldn't stay the same ♪ ♪ The muddy mystic most days is clean ♪ ♪ The banks are freshly cut and green faces ♪ ♪ Once distinctly brown are not the only ones in town ♪ ♪ These streets that once were our confines ♪ ♪ Must now embrace what gentry defines ♪ ♪ Condominium culture ♪

293
02:17:44,754 --> 02:17:51,938
[SPEAKER_06]: Bedroom convenience, university sprawl, access, egress, excess, and largesse.

294
02:17:56,641 --> 02:18:00,103
[SPEAKER_06]: Now those lowlands have become the highlights of a trending city.

295
02:18:00,483 --> 02:18:07,467
[SPEAKER_06]: And sometimes that success isn't pretty when it's at the expense of your black and brown and tan.

