[SPEAKER_06]: Squirrel nut zippers and banana splits.

320
02:20:57,281 --> 02:20:59,442
[SPEAKER_06]: Green mint juleps and button strips.

321
02:20:59,562 --> 02:21:01,743
[SPEAKER_06]: Red licorice ropes and bottle nips.

322
02:21:01,903 --> 02:21:04,604
[SPEAKER_06]: He has bazooka Joe bubblegum.

323
02:21:04,944 --> 02:21:07,305
[SPEAKER_06]: And a tiny sucker called the dum-dum.

324
02:21:07,685 --> 02:21:09,946
[SPEAKER_06]: Jawbreakers and tootsie rolls.

325
02:21:10,026 --> 02:21:12,247
[SPEAKER_06]: Sugary love for little kid souls.

326
02:21:13,188 --> 02:21:17,691
[SPEAKER_06]: Candy necklaces to wear and fight, and waxy red lips with such a sight.

327
02:21:18,272 --> 02:21:23,576
[SPEAKER_06]: Fat gum cigars and kids' cigarettes, right beside the crunchy six-lets.

328
02:21:24,156 --> 02:21:28,460
[SPEAKER_06]: Mary Jane chewies and BB bats, hot fireballs and Mexican hats.

329
02:21:28,700 --> 02:21:33,543
[SPEAKER_06]: Just the genuine Hershey's kisses, all the hits and none of the misses.

330
02:21:34,604 --> 02:21:40,669
[SPEAKER_06]: Like kids' taffy squares and Necco wafers, liquor made in Boston baked beans, gold rocks,

331
02:21:41,625 --> 02:21:46,147
[SPEAKER_06]: gum in a bag, a kid's idea of sweet tooth swag.

332
02:21:47,067 --> 02:21:50,669
[SPEAKER_06]: Before the days of Laffy Taffys, we would gobble up peppermint patties.

333
02:21:51,029 --> 02:21:56,251
[SPEAKER_06]: Before we knew about gummy bears, Twizzlers always came in pairs.

334
02:21:56,971 --> 02:22:01,413
[SPEAKER_06]: Chewy cow tails had a creamy filling, but sugar babies had top billing.

335
02:22:01,813 --> 02:22:06,595
[SPEAKER_06]: Reese's peanut butter cups had us squealing like newborn pups.

336
02:22:07,639 --> 02:22:09,441
[SPEAKER_06]: Mike and Iks and orange slices.

337
02:22:09,782 --> 02:22:12,164
[SPEAKER_06]: Saltwater taffy and tiny prices.

338
02:22:12,485 --> 02:22:15,188
[SPEAKER_06]: Lifesavers and charms and fruity flavors.

339
02:22:15,508 --> 02:22:18,351
[SPEAKER_06]: We grabbed those bags like party favors.

340
02:22:19,833 --> 02:22:23,838
[SPEAKER_06]: Chuckles were a favorite choice, and milk dust made us all rejoice.

341
02:22:23,938 --> 02:22:27,362
[SPEAKER_06]: Jolly ranchers and bitter honey, we always got a lot

342
02:22:29,526 --> 02:22:31,188
[SPEAKER_06]: Talk about kids getting excited.

343
02:22:31,508 --> 02:22:33,770
[SPEAKER_06]: You can't imagine the flame he ignited.

344
02:22:34,171 --> 02:22:38,595
[SPEAKER_06]: Our greedy fingers could barely wait to take that candy like fish take bait.

345
02:22:41,278 --> 02:22:44,221
[SPEAKER_06]: From cold January to chilly December.

346
02:22:45,253 --> 02:22:50,577
[SPEAKER_06]: More kinds of candy than I can remember at the Ville storefront on Upper Jerome.

347
02:22:51,017 --> 02:22:52,998
[SPEAKER_06]: I knew I had to write this poem.

348
