[SPEAKER_06]: Asian kid in a Tufts hoodie just whipped by in a helmet and rollerblades.

372
02:25:18,555 --> 02:25:20,396
[SPEAKER_06]: Didn't see much of that back in the day.

373
02:25:21,017 --> 02:25:26,620
[SPEAKER_06]: The university sort of, sort of hid on the hillside trying its best to be a baby Ivy.

374
02:25:27,320 --> 02:25:29,461
[SPEAKER_06]: But the co-eds come here all the time now.

375
02:25:29,961 --> 02:25:38,746
[SPEAKER_06]: Basketballs, tennis rackets, and pickleball paddles in tow on bikes, benzos, and rollerblades.

376
02:25:39,782 --> 02:25:45,569
[SPEAKER_06]: We used to bust ourselves up pretty good on rickety metal skates with clunky keys and leather straps.

377
02:25:46,470 --> 02:25:49,434
[SPEAKER_06]: Nothing a little Vaseline and Mercurochrome couldn't handle.

378
02:25:50,496 --> 02:25:52,238
[SPEAKER_06]: How did Henley put it in Invictus?

379
02:25:52,859 --> 02:25:54,581
[SPEAKER_06]: Oh yeah, bloody but unbowed.

380
02:25:59,518 --> 02:26:03,481
[SPEAKER_06]: Not too many white and off-white kids hanging out down here back then.

381
02:26:04,242 --> 02:26:10,466
[SPEAKER_06]: It was as if the invisible lines drawn to keep us in sometimes kept other folks out too.

382
02:26:11,767 --> 02:26:13,388
[SPEAKER_06]: Now they pretty much taken over.

383
02:26:14,009 --> 02:26:22,915
[SPEAKER_06]: Duggar Park, the Rhone tennis courts, the Hervey schoolyard, and a hundred addresses on Arlington, Lincoln, and Jerome.

384
02:26:24,336 --> 02:26:28,900
[SPEAKER_06]: A host of our remembered places, so few of our original faces.

385
02:26:52,152 --> 02:26:56,293
